  "id": "evolution-of-intelligence",
  "term": "evolution of intelligence",
  "definition": "Evolution of intelligence is the study of how cognitive abilities have developed across species by comparing brain size and performance on thinking tasks in relation to possible selective pressures such as environment and social organization. In primates, this approach has been used to examine similarities and differences in physical and social cognition, including evidence that human social intelligence may have evolved especially rapidly.",
